   But careful: if user already popped (vec shortened by popped handler), stack.len() matches native. If we're popping due to app reset, both native and vec need popping — do nav.pop() + stack.pop() together.
2. If stack empty → push page, push to vec.
3. top = stack.last. If top tag == route → set_child (refresh). Else if stack.len() < depth → push new page (and vec). Else → replace top (set_child + set_tag + set_title), vec unchanged.

Edge: `set_tag(Some(route))` on the top NavigationPage — but find_page(tag) won't be used anymore in this design (we use vec-based depth). Actually I can drop find_page entirely and rely on the vec. Simpler. But keep tag for the header/title display.

Now, the `popped` handler: 
```
nav.connect_popped(move |_nav, page| {
    // remove from local vec
    if let Ok(mut s) = stack.try_borrow_mut() { s.retain(|p| p.as_ref() != page.as_ref()); }
