# Plan: Generic environment values (SwiftUI-style) for the router DX

## Decision recap
- **Extend `Environment`** (no separate provider system) — it already *is* the scoped-implicit-value mechanism.
- **Generic environment values** (`.environment(key, value)` + `env.value(key)`), SwiftUI naming.
- **`NavigationApp`** host handle for env re-routing.
- Fix the one real constraint: structural slots re-render in `reconcileSlot` outside the container's `render` path.

## Core mechanism (`com.pathland.view`)

**1. `EnvironmentKey<T>`** — a typed token (SwiftUI environment-key style):
```java
public final class EnvironmentKey<T> {
    public static <T> EnvironmentKey<T> of(String name) { ... }
}
```

**2. `EnvironmentValues`** — an immutable scope chain (`key → value` + parent), O(depth) lookup:
```java
public final class EnvironmentValues {
    public static EnvironmentValues empty();
    public <T> EnvironmentValues with(EnvironmentKey<T> key, T value);
    public <T> T get(EnvironmentKey<T> key);   // nearest wins, null when absent
}
```

**3. `Environment`** gains a `VALUES` thread-local + public surface (scoping is thread-local save/restore, exactly `ButtonStyleView`):
```java
public static EnvironmentValues current();
public static void within(EnvironmentValues scope);          // set (for render scoping)
public <T> T value(EnvironmentKey<T> key);                    // instance (env.value(key))
public static <T> T value(EnvironmentKey<T> key);             // static (for body()-only composites)
```
`buttonStyle()`/`state()` stay as-is (they can migrate to values later — out of scope).

**4. Scoping modifier** — `EnvironmentMod`/`EnvironmentView` (package-private, mirrors `ButtonStyleView`) + a `View` default:
```java
default <T> View environment(EnvironmentKey<T> key, T value) { ... }  // push around subtree render, restore after
```

## Structural-slot correctness (the key constraint)

- `PathlandNode.environmentForChildren` — the scope that must apply when (re)rendering a structural slot's children.
- **`NavigationContainer.render`**: capture `incoming = Environment.current()`; set `node.environmentForChildren = incoming.with(Navigation.ROUTER, router)`; scope `ROUTER` around `selected.render(env)` (save/set/restore). Keep `node.router` for the emitter's intent resolution.
- **`ConditionalWhen.render`**: set `node.environmentForChildren = Environment.current()` (so a conditional nested in a container re-applies the ancestor `ROUTER`).
- **`Emitter.reconcileSlot`**: save `current()`, `within(slot.environmentForChildren)`, render fresh content, restore. Now destinations that `env.value(ROUTER)` work on every re-render, not just mount.

## Router application (`com.pathland.view.router`)

- **`Navigation.ROUTER`** = `public static final EnvironmentKey<Router> ROUTER = EnvironmentKey.of("router");`
- **`NavigationApp`** record: `(View root, Router router)` + `routeTo(String)` (idempotent re-route) + `of`.
- **`SplitNavDemo` becomes router-free**:
  ```java
  public static NavigationApp app(String initialPath) {
      Router router = Navigation.navigator(initialPath)
          .route("/", new HomeView()) ... .build();
      return NavigationApp.of(
          new SplitNavDemo().environment(Navigation.ROUTER, router), router);
  }
  @Override public View body() {
      Router router = Environment.value(Navigation.ROUTER);   // injected
      return HStack.of(sidebar(router), Navigation.of(router));
  }
  ```
  The sidebar reads the router via `Environment.value(ROUTER)` (scoped at the app root by `.environment`), so no constructor.

## Host (`SessionApp`, both Spring + Quarkus)
```java
this.app = SplitNavDemo.app(env.route());            // one call, router hidden
RenderResult result = emitter.mount(app.root(), new Environment(state));
...
void applyEnvironment(EnvironmentData env) {
    app.routeTo(env.route());                        // re-route encapsulated
    // viewport handling stays host-side
}
```
Drop the `Router`/`SplitNavDemo` fields; add `NavigationApp app`.

## Files
- **New**: `EnvironmentKey.java`, `EnvironmentValues.java`, `EnvironmentMod.java`/`EnvironmentView.java`, `NavigationApp.java` (+ `Environment` changes).
- **Modified**: `Environment.java`, `View.java`, `PathlandNode.java`, `Emitter.java` (`reconcileSlot`), `Navigation.java` (`ROUTER` key), `NavigationContainer.java`, `Conditional.java`, `SplitNavDemo.java`, both `SessionApp.java`, tests, `spec/DSL.md`, `status.md` ×2.

## Tests
- **pathland-view**: `.environment(key, value)` scopes + `env.value(key)` reads; nested override (inner wins); `NavigationContainer` scopes `ROUTER` to destinations; a destination that reads `env.value(ROUTER)` **re-renders correctly on route change** (reconcile re-application); `NavigationApp.of`/`routeTo` idempotent re-route.
- **demo-views**: `SplitNavDemo.app(...)` builds a seeded, mountable app; existing 5 tests keep passing.

## Verify
`mvn install`; live Spring demo curl (`/`, `/kitchen`, `/settings`, fallback) — sidebar + content render, declarative nav button works.

## Notes / out of scope
- `.navigate/.push/.replace` intents stay (emitter-resolved actions); env values cover render-time access — complementary.
- `PersistentState`/`ButtonStyle` migration to values is a later cleanup.
- Naming kept SwiftUI-style (`environment`/`value`); `EnvironmentKey` analogous to `EnvironmentValues` keys.

Ready to execute on your go.

