        return new PathlandIndexController(registry);
    }

    @Bean(destroyMethod = "shutdown")
    ... registry destroy? 
}
```
Hmm — `PathlandRegistry.shutdown()` should be called on context close. Use `@Bean(destroyMethod = "shutdown")` on the registry bean. Good.

Wait — `@ConditionalOnBean(PathlandApp.class)` on the auto-config class: Spring evaluates conditions on auto-configs after user beans are registered. Good.

The `PathlandIndexController` as a @Controller @Bean — need `@Controller` annotation on the class. And the catch-all mapping. Let me write it.

